file.content:
[
  {
    "id": "c001",
    "name": "1.1 Employment",
    "text": "1.0 Employment 1.1 Subject to the terms and conditions stated in this Employment Contract (“Contract”), the University hereby employs Michael A. Haywood as Head Football Coach of the University’s varsity intercollegiate football team (“Team”), and Michael A, Haywood hereby accepts said employment. The University and the Employee acknowledge the Employee has completed a University Employment Application form (“Application”). The Employee hereby warrants that he has filled out the Application, which is incorporated herein by reference, ina complete, accurate and truthful manner."
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "2.0 Term",
    "text": "2.0 3.0 Term The term of this Contract shall be effective on December 16, 2010, and shall expire January 15, 2016, unless otherwise extended or terminated as provided herein (“Term”). A “Contract Year” shall be the annual period of January 16 through the next ensuing January 15, during the Term; except that the first Contract Year shall begin on the effective date of this Contract and shall extend through January 15, 2012."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "Term-extension discussion",
    "text": "Ata mutually convenient time between January 15,2013 and March 31,2013, the Employee and the University’s Director of Athletics shall meet to discuss the Team, this Contract, the Employee’s performance hereunder and the desirability of a possible extension of the Term of this Contract. Atthat time, the University — in its sole discretion — may consider an extension of the Term hereof."
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "3.1 Base salary",
    "text": "Compensation and Fringe Benefits During the period in which the Employee serves as the University’s Head Football Coach: 3.] The Employee shall receive, as compensation for his services to the University and satisfactory performance of the terms and conditions of this Contract, a base Salary at the per annum rate of One Million Dollars ($1,000,000)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "3.1 Salary payment schedule",
    "text": "All such annual base salary shall be paid to the Employee in equal monthly installments, on the last day of each calendar month."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "3.2 Staff fringe benefits",
    "text": "Except as otherwise specifically and expressly set forth in this Contract, the Employee shall receive the standard staff fringe benefits received by the University's staff, as described in the University of Pittsburgh's Staff Handbook. If any such benefit is based in whole or in part upon salary paid to the Employee, such consideration shall be made without including any income other than the applicable base salary amount as described in provision 3.1 hereof,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "3.3 Club membership",
    "text": "The University shall pay initiation fees and monthly membership dues for the Employee at a mutually agreed upon golf or country club, which membership shall be used by the Employee for development and entertainment activities associated with the Employee's official responsibilities."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "3.4(1) Automobile program",
    "text": "The University shall make available to the Employee, ona loan basis, one (1) dealer-provided automobile from the car dealer program of the University’s Department of Athletics (“Department”), for the Employee’s official and personal use, fully insured by the University; provided that: (1) The University’s obligation to provide such an automobile shall cease if the dealer car program of the Department is terminated for any reason or if the Employee fails or refuses to comply fully with the University’s requirements for participation in the program."
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "3.4(2) Automobile care",
    "text": "(2) The University’s obligation to provide such an automobile shall cease if the Employee fails, at any time, properly to care for said automobile in accordance with the manufacturer’s and the dealer’s specifications and to maintain the said automobile in the same 3.5 3.6 condition existing at the time of receipt by the Employee, reasonable wear and tear excepted."
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "3.4(3) Automobile operating expenses",
    "text": "(3) The Employee shall pay all Operating expenses for the said automobile including without limitation, gasoline and oil."
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "3.4(4) Automobile records",
    "text": "(4) | The Employee shall keep, maintairi and provide to the appropriate University officials any and all written records concerning the use of the automobile as may be required by the University."
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "3.4 Automobile return",
    "text": "If at any time the University reasonably determines the Employee has failed or refused to comply with any of the above-stated requirements, the Employee shall return the automobile to the University, immediately upon the request of the University, and the Employee shall have no right to receive any other automobile from, or through, the University."
  },
  {
    "id": "c013",
    "name": "3.5 Game tickets",
    "text": "During each Contract Year, the University shall provide the Employee, atno cost to him, six (6) season tickets for the Team's home games, and six (6) tickets for any away game in which the Team participates, all of which shall be used for his official responsibilities."
  },
  {
    "id": "c014",
    "name": "3.6 Expense reimbursement",
    "text": "The University shall reimburse the Employee for appropriate travel and outof-pocket expenses reasonably incurred by him for the purpose of and in connection with the performance of his duties under this Contract, including but not limited to NCAA approved expenses incurred while recruiting and scouting. All such reimbursement shall be made in accordance with the standard procedures of the University upon presentation to the University of vouchers or other statements itemizing such expenses in reasonable detail."
  },
  {
    "id": "c015",
    "name": "3.7 Supplemental compensation",
    "text": "3.7 While the Employee is serving as the University’s Head Football Coach under this Contract, he shall be entitled to receive supplemental compensation in consideration for his efforts in contributing to the exceptional performance of the Team and for the extra services required of the Employee in preparation for and participation in post-season games of the Team. Specifically, the Employee shall be entitled to the following: A. The greatest of: (1) (2) (3) One Hundred Fifty Thousand ($ 150,000) for a Contract Year in which the Team wins the post-season national championship game, played as a part of the national Bow] Championship Series, or similar successor series; or One Hundred Thousand Dollars ($100,000) for a Contract Year in which the Team participates in, but loses, the post-season national championship game, played as a part of the national Bowl Championship Series, or similar successor series; or One Hundred Thousand Dollars $100,000) for a Contract Year in which the Team participates in one of the post-season bowl games ~ other than the national championship game — generally considered a part of the national Bowl Championship Series, or similar successor series; and seventy Five Thousand Dollars ($75,000) fora Contract Year in which the Team wins the championship football game (if any) or (if there is no such championship game) is generally recognized as the regular season football champion of the Big East Conference (or such other 1 3.8 applicable athletics conference in which the University is then a member, affiliated with and/or competes); and C. Seventy-Five Thousand Dollars ($75,000) for a Contract Year in which the Employee is named national coach of the year by the Associated Press, ESPN, USA Today or other similar nationally-recognized Organization or outlet teasonably acceptable to the University’s Director of Athletics."
  },
  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "3.7 Supplemental-compensation payment date",
    "text": "All such additional compensation shall be paid on or before the March 15 next following any of the events requiring such payment(s),"
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "3.8 Shoe/Apparel/Equipment Contracts",
    "text": "The parties agree that the University, and not the Employee, shall have the sole and exclusive right and opportunity to enter into a contract, or contracts, with any and all shoe/ apparel /equipment/ supplies /accessories manufacturers and/or distributors for the purpose of committing any or all of the University’s intercollegiate athletics teams, including the Team, to wear or use particular shoes, apparel, equipment, supplies or accessories during practices, games and/or official Team events and activities; and/or for the purpose of committing the Employee (and/or other University employees) to wear, use, promote, endorse Or consult with the manufacturer(s), distributor(s) and/or seller(s) concerning the design or marketing of such shoes, apparel, equipment, supplies or accessories (eacha “Shoe/Apparel/Equipment Contract”)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "3.8 Employee cooperation",
    "text": "The Employee shall cooperate fully with the University in the University’s efforts to enter into, and to comply with, any and every such Shoe / Apparel/Equipment Contract, including but not limited to participating in such promotional activities as are required in any and every such Shoe/ Apparel / Equipment Contract."
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "3.9 Shoe/Apparel/Equipment revenue and compensation",
    "text": "Any and all revenue resulting from any Shoe/Apparel/ Equipment Contract shall be the sole and exclusive property of the University. Nonetheless, for services rendered by the Employee in connection with any such contracts, while the Employee is representing the University as Head Football Coach the Employee shall be paid by the University, the sum of One Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars ($150,000) per year, during each Contract Year. The applicable amounts shall be payable to the Employee, in each Contract Year, in two (2) equal installments to be paid on or before the first day of September and the first day of January (by January 1, 2012 for the first Contract Year)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "Publicity rights",
    "text": "In relation to the subject of, and the matters described in, this provision 3.8, and for the purpose of promoting the Team and the University’s intercollegiate athletics program generally, the Employee hereby consents to, acknowledges and agrees that the University shall have the right (and shall be permitted to assign such right to others) to use the Employee’s name, nickname, likeness (actual, simulated, caricature or otherwise), ima Ze, voice, personality, signature and/or other publicity right."
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "Stadium box",
    "text": "Subject to the facility owner’s standard conditions, the Employee shall, in addition to the tickets described in provision 3.5, be provided the complimentary use of a private stadium box, as assigned or re-assigned by the University, for and during each of the University’s home football games at Heinz Field, Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania."
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "4.1 Full Time and Attention",
    "text": "Full Time and Attention 4] While employed as the University’s Head Football Coach, the Employee shall devote his full time, attention and energies to his duties as Head Footbal] Coach, including such related duties in the intercollegiate athletics program of the University as may be assigned to him by the University’s Director of Athletics, subject to any exceptions hereinafter expressly described. He shall also select such assistants and applicable staff, as authorized by the University, who shall be committed, likewise, to devoting their full time, attention and energies to the furtherance of the athletics program of the University. The Employee shall comply fully with the legislation, rules, regulations and policies of the National Collegiate Athletic Association (“NCAA”), of the Big East Conference (or such other applicable athletics conference in which the University is then a member, affiliated with and/or competes) of the University and of the Department (including without limitation the mission statements of the University and of the Department and the principles of “The Pitt Promise”), and he shall take every precaution to ensure that all members of his staff comply fully with such legislation, rules, regulations and policies."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "5.1 Direction of Director of Athletics",
    "text": "Direction of Director of Athletics and Duties of the Employee During the period in which the Employee serves as the University’s Head Football Coach: 5.1 The Employee's immediate supervisor, for purposes of implementing this Contract, shall be the Director of Athletics of the University, and all matters pertaining to the operation of the University’s athletics program including, but not limited to, those set forth in provisions 5.2 and 5.3 below, shall be subject to the direction and control of the said Director of Athletics."
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "5.2 Performance evaluations",
    "text": "The Employee shall cooperate with performance evaluation(s) of his performance to be conducted in the same manner and on the same basis as performance evaluations are conducted for other University staff, taking into account this Contract, prior performance evaluations of the Employee and the expectations and goals previously agreed upon by the Employee and the University’s Director of Athletics."
  },
  {
    "id": "c025",
    "name": "5.3 Employee duties",
    "text": "In addition to other duties as described in this Contract, the Employee shall give proper time and attention to, and shall perform in good faith and to the best of his ability, the following duties: (1) promoting the athletic, academic and social welfare of the student-athletes in his charge; (2) recruiting, teaching, supervising and evaluating student-athletes in his charge; (3) recruiting, teaching, supervising and evaluating the performance of assistant coaches and other football staff members; (4) managing the Team budget; (5) complying with NCAA legislation, rules, regulations and policies (“NCAA Rules”); (6) avoiding the imposition of any academic disincentive penalty on the Team, as described in NCAA Rules (by way of example only, pursuant to an NCAA academic performance program); (7) maintaining a good working relationship.with the University community; (8) conducting public relations related to the University’s football program, including relations with media, alumni, boosters and the general public which reflect positively on the University; and (9) such other duties as assigned from time to time by the University’s Director of Athletics."
  },
  {
    "id": "c026",
    "name": "5.4 NCAA discipline",
    "text": "Without limiting any other provision of this Contract, if the Employee is found to be in, or to have been in, violation of NCAA Rules, either while employed by the University (in any capacity, pursuant to this Contract or otherwise) or during prior employment at another NCAA member 6.0 7.0 institution, the Employee shall be subject to disciplinary or corrective action as set forth in the provisions of the NCAA enforcement procedures, including suspension without pay or termination of employment for significant or repetitive violations."
  },
  {
    "id": "c027",
    "name": "6.1 Academic policy",
    "text": "University Academic and Athletic Policy During the period in which the Employee serves as the University’s Head Football Coach: 6.1 6.2 The Employee shall recognize that the primary mission of the University is education, and the Employee shall perform his duties as described herein and administer the University’s football program with proper regard for the academic welfare of the student-athletes in the University’s football program and fully consistent with the academic standards and policies of the University. The Employee shall perform his duties as described herein and administer the University’s football program in accordance with academic policies established by the University’s Chancellor and the University’s Board of Trustees,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c028",
    "name": "6.2 Athletics policy",
    "text": "Overall athletics policy shall remain the exclusive prerogative of the University. The Employee shall perform under this Contract and administer the University’s football program in accordance with athletics policies established by the University’s Chancellor and the University’s Board of Trustees."
  },
  {
    "id": "c029",
    "name": "7.1 Decisions Affecting Football Program",
    "text": "Decisions Affecting Football Program During the period in which the Employee serves as the University’s Head Football Coach: 10 8.0 7.1 The University, through its Director of Athletics, shall permit the Employee to offer input on decisions relating to choice and scheduling of the Team’s opponents, means of travel to be employed by the Team, hotel and food accommodations applicable to the Team, size and content of the Team’s traveling squad, and other matters pertaining to the operation of the Team, but final decisions in all such matters shall rest with the University’s Director of Athletics."
  },
  {
    "id": "c030",
    "name": "8.1 Marketing and appearances",
    "text": "Marketing/Appearances/Television, Radio and Other Programs During the period in which the Employee serves as the University’s Head Football Coach: 8.1 The Employee shall make himself available for, participate in and cooperate fully with the University’s marketing and promotion of the Team and the University’s intercollegiate athletics program, and with media and other public and private appearances, at such times and places as the University may reasonably require. Further, the Employee shall make himself available for, participate in and cooperate fully with public and private fund raising and development activities at such times and places as the University may reasonably require — which activities may include, but shall not be limited to , cultivation of donors and potential donors to the University and events organized by sponsors of the University."
  },
  {
    "id": "c031",
    "name": "8.2 Programs",
    "text": "8.2 The Employee shall make himself available for, participate in and cooperate fully with the production and marketing of any and all shows and programs (including but not limited to call-in shows and specials relating to playoff or bowl games) distributed via terrestrial radio, satellite radio, television, internet, computer, mobile device, wireless device and/or any other media in which the subject is, in whole or in part, the Team and/or University 11 8.3 8.4 intercollegiate athletics (the “Programs”), as arranged by the University or the University’s designee (including but not limited to ISP Sports, LLC)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c032",
    "name": "8.3 Program services and rights",
    "text": "The Employee shall perform such reasonable services as may be requested by the University, or the University’s designee, and/or as may be specified in the University’s or the University’s designee’s contract(s) with the producers and distributors of Programs. The Employee shall not appear on or in any competing shows or programs without the prior written consent of the University’s Director of Athletics. As between the University and the Employee, the University shall own any and all intellectual property and other rights in and to such Programs."
  },
  {
    "id": "c033",
    "name": "8.4 Program revenue and compensation",
    "text": "Any and all revenue resulting from the Programs, and other matters described in provisions 8.1, 8.2 and 8.3, shall be the sole and exclusive property of the University. Nonetheless, for services rendered by the Employee in connection therewith, while the Employee is representing the University as Head Football Coach the Employee shall be paid by the University, the sum of Three Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars ($350,000) per year, during each Contract Year. The applicable amounts shall be paid to the Employee, in each Contract Year, in two (2) equal installments to be paid on or before the first day of September and the first day of January (by January 1, 2012 for the first Contract Year)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c034",
    "name": "Program publicity rights",
    "text": "In relation to the Programs, the other matters described in provisions 8.1 and 8.2, above, and for the purpose of promoting the Team and the University’s intercollegiate athletics program generally, the Employee hereby consents to, acknowledges and agrees that the University shall have the right (and shall"
  },
  {
    "id": "c035",
    "name": "9.1 Football-camp requirements",
    "text": "form acceptable to the University; naming the University as an additional insured; providing the University with a copy of each certificate of insurance for such insurance; and, at the University’s discretion, entering into a written contract upon standard University terms for similar third-party uses of University facilities, including the obligation to indemnify, defend and hold harmless the University from any loss."
  },
  {
    "id": "c036",
    "name": "9.2 Football-camp facilities",
    "text": "The Employee shall consult with the University’s Director of Athletics no Jater than ten (10) months in advance of any planned football camp(s) regarding the availability of the athletics facilities the Employee desires to use. Once the University has agreed to make specific facilities available for any particular football camp(s), it shall not change the applicable facilities arrangement for the particular camp(s) unless it gives the Employee at least ninety (90) days’ notice (in which case it will incur no liability for the change) or the Employee consents to the change. The Employee shall not unreasonably withhold consent when reasonable alternative facilities are offered by the University."
  },
  {
    "id": "c037",
    "name": "9.3 Football-camp terms",
    "text": "The University shall deal with the Employee on matters concerning the football camp(s) under terms and conditions consistent with those then established by the NCAA for the operation of college football camps."
  },
  {
    "id": "c038",
    "name": "9.4 Football-camp records",
    "text": "The Employee shall maintain, keep and retain such accurate and complete financial, and other, records concerning such camps as the University may, from time to time, request. Upon receipt of a request by the University, the Employee shall provide access to such records, and to all other camp records, within ten (10) days."
  },
  {
    "id": "c039",
    "name": "9.5 Football camps after termination",
    "text": "9.5 In the event of termination of this Contract by either party, or expiration hereof, the University shall be under no obligation to permit any football camp to be held by the Employee, after the effective date of such termination or expiration (whether or not one has been planned), and the University shall be released from all obligations relating thereto immediately upon such termination or expiration."
  },
  {
    "id": "c040",
    "name": "10.1 Outside Business Activities",
    "text": "10.0 Outside Business Activities 10.1 While serving as the University’s Head Football Coach, the Employee shall be prohibited from publicly using, and shall be prohibited from permitting or licensing any other person or entity publicly to use, the Employee’s name, nickname, likeness (actual, simulated, caricature or otherwise), image, voice, personality, signature and/or other publicity right to market, promote, advertise, sponsor, sell or endorse any product, good, service, cause or position without the prior written approval of the University’s Director of Athletics and the University’s Chancellor. Without limiting the foregoing, the Employee shall be permitted to contract independently with outside sources for separate and additional compensation which shall inure to his benefit, subject to the prior written approval of the University’s Director of Athletics and the University’s Chancellor. The Employee shall not permit the use of any of the University’s names, logos, symbols, designs, colors, team names, nicknames, mascots, slogans, abbreviations, trademarks or service marks in any such activities without the prior written approval of the University’s Director of Athletics and the University’s Chancellor. To the extent the University’s facilities or other property may be desired by the Employee for use in such activities (which shall require the prior approval of the University’s Director of Athletics), the Employee shall first 15 enter into a separate written contract for the same on terms and conditions acceptable to the University."
  },
  {
    "id": "c041",
    "name": "10.1(A) University Obligations Are Primary",
    "text": "The Employee's participation in any and all such outside business activities shall, further, be subject to the following: A. University Obligations Are Primary. Such outside activities shall not interfere with the full and complete performance by the Employee of his duties and obligations as a University employee, recognizing always that the Employee's primary obligations are to the University."
  },
  {
    "id": "c042",
    "name": "10.1(B) NCAA, Conference and University Rules Control",
    "text": "NCAA, Conference and University Rules Control. Inno event shall the Employee accept or receive directly or indirectly any monies, benefits or any other gratuity whatsoever from any person, corporation, University booster club or alumni association or other benefactor if such action would violate NCAA Rules or the Big East Conference's (or such other applicable athletics conference in which the University is then a member, affiliated with and/or competes) or the University’s constitution, mission, legislation, bylaws, rules, policies or regulations. Changes in such NCAA Rules or the applicable conference’s or the University’s constitution, mission, legislation, bylaws, rules, policies or regulations or interpretations thereof shall automatically apply to this Contract without the necessity of a written modification."
  },
  {
    "id": "c043",
    "name": "10.1(C) University Is Not Liable",
    "text": "University Is Not Liable. Such activities are independent of the Employee's University employment, and the University shall haveno responsibility or liability for any claims arising therefrom. The Employee further agrees to indemnify, defend and hold harmless the University and its trustees, employees, agents, officers and assigns from and against any and all suits, judgments, actions, causes of 16 action, claims, demands, liabilities, injuries, losses, damages, expenses and costs (including but not limited to attorney's fees) which arise from, are caused by or are associated with the Employee's, his employees’, contractors’, assigns’ or agents’, performance of any such outside activities or contracts."
  },
  {
    "id": "c044",
    "name": "10.1(D) Employee Retains all Revenues",
    "text": "D. Employee Retains all Revenues. Except for the limitations on such outside compensation as established by or set forth in this Contract or in the constitution, mission, le gislation, bylaws, rules, policies and/or regulations and interpretations thereof of the University, or the Big East Conference (or such other applicable athletics conference in which the University is then a member, affiliated with and/or competes) or the NCAA, the Employee shall be entitled to retain all revenue generated by such outside activities, The Employee, in accordance with NCAA Rules, shall provide a detailed written report (at least annually and no later than the date(s) the University’s Director of Athletics shall designate) of all athletically related income and benefits from sources outside the University (including, but not limited to, income from annuities, sports camps, housing benefits, country club memberships, complimentary ticket sales, television and radio programs and endorsement or consultation contracts with athletic shoe, apparel or equipment manufa cturers) to the University’s Director of Athletics and the University’s Chancellor."
  },
  {
    "id": "c045",
    "name": "10.1(E) University Opportunities",
    "text": "E. University Opportunities. In no event shall the Employee be permitted to usurp any corporate opportunities of the University or engage in any activity causing a conflict of interest with his University employment."
  },
  {
    "id": "c046",
    "name": "10.1(F) University Policy",
    "text": "F, University Policy. Further, the approval of all athletically related income and benefits shall be consistent with the University’s polices 17 then in effect related to outside income and benefits applicable to other University full-time or part-time staff."
  },
  {
    "id": "c047",
    "name": "11.1 Vacation entitlement",
    "text": "11.0 Vacation 11.1 Ineach Contract Year, the Employee shall be entitled to twenty (20) days of vacation (equivalent of four (4) working weeks), with compensation, so long as the timing of use of any such vacation is approved, in advance, by the University’s Director of Athletics."
  },
  {
    "id": "c048",
    "name": "11.1 Unused vacation",
    "text": "All such vacation time must be used by the Employee prior to the termination or expiration of this Contract. The Employee shall not be permitted to retain any such unused vacation time after the expiration or termination date of this Contract (for example during a renewal term of this Contract, if any) and shall be entitled to no compensation for any unused vacation time."
  },
  {
    "id": "c049",
    "name": "11.1 Exclusive vacation terms",
    "text": "The foregoing paragraphs of this provision 11.1 shall exclusively govern matiers pertaining to the Employee’s vacation time, notwithstanding anything contained herein or in University rules, regulations or policies to the contrary."
  },
  {
    "id": "c050",
    "name": "12.1 Assistant coaches and staff",
    "text": "12.0 AssistantFootball Coaches and Other Football Staff 12.1 While employed in the capacity of Head Football Coach, the Employee shall have authority to select, hire, establish the salaries of, and dismiss assistant football coaches, a Director of High School Relations and a Director of Football Operations, all subject to the prior approval of the University’s Director of Athletics, in accordance with University policy, and to direct the scope of their duties."
  },
  {
    "id": "c051",
    "name": "12.1 Director of Football Operations reporting",
    "text": "The said Director of Football Operations shall have a 18 dual reporting relationship to the Head Football Coach and to the University’s Director of Athletics."
  },
  {
    "id": "c052",
    "name": "12.1 Staff budget",
    "text": "The parties hereby agree that the University’s allotted budget for the costs of employment of all such individuals shall not be less than One Million Nine Hundred Thousand Dollars ($1,900,000) per Contract Year, and the Employee shall ensure the costs of employment of all such individuals shall remain within the University's allotted budget for said purposes."
  },
  {
    "id": "c053",
    "name": "13.1 Additional Services",
    "text": "13.0 Additional Services 13.1 Upon the recommendation of the Employee, but subject to the prior approval of the University’s Director of Athletics, each University assistant football coach designated by the Employee may be paid an additional one (1) month’s salary, at the rate then in effect for each such assistant to compensate the assistant for additional services rendered with re gard to any post-season bowl game, during the Term, to which the Team is invited and participates. Such recommendations shall be made to the Director of Athletics no later than the January 15 immediately following the conclusion of each such postseason bowl game. All such properly approved compensation shall be paid on or before the March 31 next following each such post-season bow] game."
  },
  {
    "id": "c054",
    "name": "Section 14.1 — Just-cause termination and cessation of obligations",
    "text": "14.1 Notwithstanding any other provisions hereof, the University may at any time, with just cause, terminate this Contract or suspend the Employee with or without pay. In the event of such termination, the University shall be relieved of all further obligations (financial and otherwise) to Employee. Termination of this Contract for just cause shall not prohibit the University from pursuing any and all other legal rights or remedies available to it."
  },
  {
    "id": "c055",
    "name": "14.1 Just-cause definition",
    "text": "For the purposes of this Contract, “just cause” shall mean, in addition to its normally understood meaning in employment contracts, any one or more of the following: A, any conduct by Employee resulting in his conviction of a violation of a criminal statute: or any violation of NCAA Rules by Employee, while employed by the University (in any capacity, pursuant to this Contract or otherwise) or while he was previously employed at another NCAA member institution; or any violation of NCAA Rules by any coach; employee; staff member; student-athlete; or representative of his institution’s athletics interests, with Employee’s prior knowledge and consent, or of which Employee reasonably should have known and prevented, or of which Employee learned at any time but failed to report to his institution, while Employee is employed by the University (in any capacity, pursuant to this Contract or otherwise) or while he was previously employed at another NCAA member institution; or misappropriation or misuse of University funds by Employee; or any breach of Employee’s warranties, duties or obligations described in this Contract; or as determined by the University, any conduct of Employee that is seriously prejudicial to the best interests of the University or its intercollegiate athletics program; that violates the University’s or the 20 Department’s then-current mission; that brings the University into disrepute; or that reflects dishonesty, disloyalty, willful misconduct, gross negligence, moral turpitude or refusal or unwillingness to perform his duties; or G. any conduct by Employee that violates or breaches the published mission, rules, regulations or policies of the University or the Department."
  },
  {
    "id": "c056",
    "name": "14.2 Termination without just cause",
